  "description": "Rainwater absorbs carbon dioxide and becomes a weak acid that dissolves limestone through its cracks; over thousands or millions of years the cracks become caves. Inside, every drop leaves calcite: stalactites grow from the ceiling and stalagmites from the floor, very slowly, until they join into columns. Son Doong cave in Vietnam is so big it has its own jungle. Original 3D animation.",
